Subject: [WASM research] keep browser stdio QMP on the main-loop context

Select the existing non-I/O-thread QMP path for Emscripten stdio only.
The browser's stdio data and poll callbacks live on the UI thread.  The r16
negative control kept both guest heartbeats and the QEMU main loop alive,
but stopped invoking the independent QMP context's stdin poll at about 7 s;
the later screendump remained unread in the JS queue and never entered its
QMP handler.  That narrows the observed failure to the independent QMP
I/O/context path, without establishing the underlying GLib failure cause.

This is an explicit host I/O-thread configuration.  Native builds, other
chardevs, guest vCPU threads, QMP parsing/dispatch/response, framebuffer
production and controller data planes retain their existing paths.  The
stdio greeting no longer offers out-of-band commands because the existing
QMP implementation ties that capability to use_io_thread; in-band QMP is
unchanged.  No keepalive, periodic QMP, synthetic values or timing fix is
introduced.  Two sequential guests and repeated start/frame/cleanup remain
required runtime acceptance; this patch alone is not validation.

The selected stdio main-context branch emits one startup info marker after
its handlers are installed, for same-runtime/session evidence binding.
Apply after 0011 on the same frozen native31 browser source.

--- a/monitor/qmp.c
+++ b/monitor/qmp.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "chardev/char-io.h"
 #include "monitor-internal.h"
 #include "qapi/error.h"
+#include "qemu/error-report.h"
 #include "qapi/qapi-commands-control.h"
 #include "qapi/qmp/qdict.h"
 #include "qapi/qmp/qjson.h"
@@ -513,6 +514,7 @@
 void monitor_init_qmp(Chardev *chr, bool pretty, Error **errp)
 {
     MonitorQMP *mon = g_new0(MonitorQMP, 1);
+    bool use_io_thread;
 
     if (!qemu_chr_fe_init(&mon->common.chr, chr, errp)) {
         g_free(mon);
@@ -521,8 +523,18 @@
     qemu_chr_fe_set_echo(&mon->common.chr, true);
 
     /* Note: we run QMP monitor in I/O thread when @chr supports that */
-    monitor_data_init(&mon->common, true, false,
-                      qemu_chr_has_feature(chr, QEMU_CHAR_FEATURE_GCONTEXT));
+    use_io_thread = qemu_chr_has_feature(chr, QEMU_CHAR_FEATURE_GCONTEXT);
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    /*
+     * Browser stdio is a main-thread JS input bridge.  Keep its QMP watch on
+     * the existing main-loop context instead of an independent GLib loop.
+     * Other chardevs retain their native I/O-thread selection.
+     */
+    if (object_dynamic_cast(OBJECT(chr), TYPE_CHARDEV_STDIO)) {
+        use_io_thread = false;
+    }
+#endif
+    monitor_data_init(&mon->common, true, false, use_io_thread);
 
     mon->pretty = pretty;
 
@@ -549,5 +561,11 @@
                                  monitor_qmp_read, monitor_qmp_event,
                                  NULL, &mon->common, NULL, true);
         monitor_list_append(&mon->common);
-    }
-}
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+        if (object_dynamic_cast(OBJECT(chr), TYPE_CHARDEV_STDIO)) {
+            info_report("M5_WASM_QMP_CONTEXT stdio=1 context=main-loop "
+                        "use_io_thread=0 oob_offered=0");
+        }
+#endif
+    }
+}
